{"custom_id":"s-ap_statistics-m09-k0","ok":true,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfypcFadCJDfzMaP6N7dJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here 912.2 falls inside the 90% confidence interval, so we don't reject H0.\n\n**Why the interval matches this test:** a two-sided 90% confidence interval leaves 5% in each tail. That lines up with a one-sided test at α = 0.05.\n\n**Check with the numbers:**\n- Sample mean x̄ = (894.1 + 937.9) / 2 = 916.0\n- Margin of error = 21.9\n- With df = 21, t* = 1.721, so the standard error is SE = 21.9 / 1.721 ≈ 12.73\n- t = (916.0 − 912.2) / 12.73 ≈ 0.30, which gives p ≈ 0.38\n\nSince p ≈ 0.38 > 0.05, we fail to reject H0. There is not convincing evidence that μ > 912.2. The answer is choice index 3."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CeSh6ke7oYQN9xFtXYUsTH","name":"submit_solution","input":{"answers":[{"item":"1","choice_index":3,"final_answer":"Fail to reject H0","brief_reasoning":"The 90% CI matches a one-sided test at α=0.05, and 912.2 is inside the interval. Here x̄=916, SE≈12.73, t≈0.30, p≈0.38 > 0.05.","ambiguous_or_flawed":false}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":459,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null},"usage":{"input_tokens":432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":459,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"cost":0.011135200000000001}
